From 425f8bed49d1792433c86f9c521fe06ba66097af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:47:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cms): give department activities their own article,
 news-style
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adopts the News Post mechanism for department activities instead of just
visually resembling it:

- departmentActivity gains a slug, a full localized rich-text body
  (identical shape to newsPost's), an optional author/byline, and a cover
  photo caption — the same fields newsPost uses to build a full article.
- The Activities & Milestones cards on the department detail page are now
  wired exactly like the Newsroom's cards: clickable image, title link,
  "Read more" with the arrow icon, all pointing at
  /departments/:deptId/activities/:slug.
- New DepartmentActivityDetail page mirrors NewsDetail.tsx: hero image
  with lightbox, date/author meta, PortableText body rendering, share bar,
  and a "More Activities & Milestones" related grid scoped to the same
  department — reusing the existing PortableContent and ImageLightbox
  components rather than duplicating their logic.
- An activity with no body falls back to showing its short summary, and
  an unknown slug falls back to the first activity, matching how
  NewsDetail already behaves.

Still fully Sanity-controlled and hidden until a department has published
activities — no fallback/sample content invented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
